## Comparison: Quicksort vs Merge Sort

| Feature | Quicksort | Merge Sort |
|---------|-----------|------------|
| **Time Complexity** | O(n log n) avg, O(n²) worst | O(n log n) always |
| **Space Complexity** | O(log n) | O(n) |
| **Stable** | No | Yes |
| **In-place** | Yes | No |
| **Best For** | General purpose | Stable sorting, linked lists |

## When to Use Each

- **Use Quicksort:** When memory is limited, need in-place sorting
- **Use Merge Sort:** When stability is required, or guaranteed performance is needed

This implementation provides a clear, educational example of merge sort with comprehensive comments and multiple test cases for verification, matching the style and detail level of the quicksort implementation.
